      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b95b17f008a5157ae406b0e|full_name}: This. There's other concerning things like crashers and DDoSers but these we can deal with ourselves with the self-moderation featues we were given. I'd rather the team focuses on the IK system over security since IK is what brings the avatars of others to life. It's what makes everyone interactable. The whole purpose of IK is to convince the third party that they are not talking to a interpolated, stuttering, infrequently updating puppet and right now this system is not doing it's job.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
